<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Angkor Thom</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a> Thom was a walled royal city built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayavarman-vii">Jayavarman VII</a> in the late twelfth century. At its centre stands the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayon">Bayon</a> temple, famous for its many carved stone faces. It is one of the major monuments of the Khmer Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/angkor-thom.jpg" alt="Angkor Thom" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This Photo was taken by Supanut Arunoprayote. … · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Angkor_Thom_(II).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…sack of Angkor by Cham forces in 1177 exposed the empire's vulnerability, but Jayavarman VII drove out the invaders, defeating them in a celebrated naval battle on the Tonle Sap, enclosed his new capital of <b>Angkor Thom</b> within massive walls and moat, and subjugated Champa itself in 1203.</blockquote><a href="/empire/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Chams sacked Angkor in 1178, Jayavarman VII restored the empire, built a new capital at <b>Angkor Thom</b> with the Bayon as its state temple, and dedicated it to Buddhism, encouraged by his wife Indradevi, a devout Mahayana Buddhist.</blockquote><a href="/work/angkor-wat">Angkor Wat · Reception</a></li><li><blockquote>In the reign of Jayavarman VII alone Ta Prohm, Preah Khan, Banteay Kdei and Neak Pean were built, beside the Bayon at the centre of <b>Angkor Thom</b>.</blockquote><a href="/societies/khmer-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Khmer Empire</a></li></ul></section>
